Z||000003||Formula88||08-27-2001||12:13 PM||||Are the GT trumpet tips chrome or polished stainless steel?  I've heard both.  I've got a pair that need resurrection, so I want to know what kind of cleaner/polish to use without damaging them.  <P>Also, it looks like the tips are just the trumpet cones put over the regular exhaust tips.  Does anyone know if that's how they did it, or if the exhaust pipe is different under the cone?||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||08-27-2001||12:21 PM||||The stock GT tips are stainless steel and can be amazingly cleaned up using steel wool or similiar abrasive product!  I have Pacesetter Monza resonator tips on my GT... they had them in Gold which compliments the Green great.  They are the only form of "Muffler" I have on my car, so It's loud and roars beautifully.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||08-27-2001||12:32 PM||||To clean the GT tips I used watered down rubbing compound, Then polished with Mother's mag polish. They came out looking like mirror chrome. If your looking for different style tips, Jeg's sells all the different styles of Bola tips. Kind of $$$$ but they are hard chromed and polish up great. The Ocelot tips are soft chromed and require constant care if using the car for daily driving.||||reg||1
